@back bg_squareAfternoon
NA: That theater, that city, and those people.

NA: Some names survived.

NA: Others did not.

NA: There was a time when an alferes tried to start a revolution.

NA: A man with a curious name.

NA: Tiradentes.

NA: The movement failed, but he became a martyr.

NA: His name spanned centuries.

NA: It was remembered, studied, and turned into a symbol.

NA: Other comrades were imprisoned, exiled.

NA: Sent to distant lands.

NA: Some survived, others slowly faded from memory.

NA: But no fate seemed as cruel as the one that awaited a simple artist.

NA: A person who never desired revolutions.

NA: Nor glory or power.

NA: Just the freedom to exist.

NA: Just the right to be.

NA: Celina, Célio... Cel.

NA: None of the names remained in the books.

NA: No record tells their story.

NA: No public square bears their name.

NA: No statue was erected.

NA: As if they had never existed.

NA: As if the world had decided to forget them.

NA: And perhaps it would have succeeded, had you forgotten them too.

NA: But you didn't.

NA: Because you can still see them.

NA: In your memories.

NA: Sitting backstage, dancing alone at the overlook, laughing at their own jokes.
